  "notes": "GAAP city. Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement Total column (p6); business-type from the proprietary statement Total Fund column (pp9-10). Governmental 'Taxes' 151,840 (General 105,503 + Debt Service 46,337) kept as one line, category taxes: the Statement of Activities 'Taxes - property' 154,684 does not tie. Ending cash = Cash + Cash with County Treasurer from the governmental funds balance sheet (p5); restricted cash 414,237 excluded; no beginning cash printed. Proceeds from sale of assets 4,765 in other_financing. Governmental transfers in 317,705 / out 42,705 (net 275,000 from the Electric 75,000 and Sewer 200,000 transfers out). Business 'Other' operating revenue is not in charges for services on the Statement of Activities (Miscellaneous 19,290 there), kept other. Statement of Activities business expenses by fund (Electric 814,627, Water 192,438, Refuse 105,491; total 1,245,725) differ from the proprietary statement (814,177, 192,152, 106,226; total 1,245,724); proprietary statement used. Governmental roll: 474,041 + 810,249 - 589,349 + 317,705 - 42,705 + 4,765 = 974,706. Business: 1,068,953 + 1,339,414 - 1,245,724 - 275,000 = 887,643. Only supplementary schedule is a combined all-funds cash-basis budgetary comparison (p13), so detail is one line per individual fund column of the governmental funds (p6) and proprietary funds (pp9-10) statements; proprietary detail totals add nonoperating interest to the printed operating totals. Capital outlay: Street Fund column labelled Capital Outlay: Streets/Highways (fund names the function); General and Nonmajor columns print no function, labelled Capital outlay. Intergovernmental lines kept as other state aid (no highway allocation printed). Read pages 1-13 of 13"
}
